## Step 2 — Probe frame arrays, value results, and project loading

Loaded the vendored tools with `installVendor({ reference: true })` and used in-memory Typed snippets. `node --input-type=module` with a resolution hook for the unbuilt sources failed on a parameter property with `ERR_UNSUPPORTED_TYPESCRIPT_SYNTAX`. Reran with `node --experimental-transform-types --input-type=module` and the same hook.

The default `Program.fromProject` ingest reported `unknown tape opcode 252 at 9` for the 64-word frame array. A version using a scalar in place of the array ingested, and `createWb(...).projects.open('"'probe')"'` ingested the original source with tape metadata. Direct tape ingest confirmed correct wraparound, rotates, and a four-word result. An attempt to call `p.compile` on the kernel returned `TypeError: p.compile is not a function`. Used `lowerToImage` and `runImage` for the kernel probe.

- The evaluator, default-policy reference image, and checked `speed` image wrote `[0, 32768, 0, 65535, 48879]` and returned `-1091576147`. The follow-up generated check agreed on all 16 calls without traps or limits.
- Calling the four-word helper directly from the reference image returned only the first word with the runner'"'s existing arguments. Supplying the signatures gave all four.
- A 55-cell word-packing loop returned "'`0x41414100` on both the evaluator and reference image in 610 statements and 1,586 instructions respectively. A probe of an explicit `: void` annotation produced `unknown type void`. The design uses the first output word as the scalar result.
- The framework SHA-256 function returned the empty-string and `abc` digests found in the identity tests.

## Step 3 — Write the implementation design

Chose one padded ASCII block for SHA-256 so the framework'"'s text hash can check every generated case. Chose a four-word value-record helper and scalar state for ChaCha20 so the eight calls in a double round share one implementation and keep register pressure visible. Both kernels measure instructions per 64-byte block.

Documented the loader metadata and reference signature changes, linked seven source files through docmgr, and marked the statement counts as estimates for the eventual kernels. The feature probes executed only small in-memory fixtures.
